# Brownies

Based on [https://tasty.co/recipe/…](https://tasty.co/recipe/the-best-one-bowl-brownies) ([wayback](http://web.archive.org/web/20251122165149/https://tasty.co/recipe/the-best-one-bowl-brownies))

{ rating="4" image="brownies.jpeg" }
:::
:::

## Ingredients

- [ ] 1 cup [unsalted butter]{ ing="unsalted-butter" }, 2 sticks
- [ ] 4 oz [semi-sweet chocolate bar]{ ing="semi-sweet-chocolate-bar" }, coarsely chopped
- [ ] 1.5 cups [granulated sugar]{ ing="granulated-sugar" }
- [ ] 3/4 cup [brown sugar]{ ing="brown-sugar" }
- [ ] 1 Tbsp [vanilla extract]{ ing="vanilla-extract" }
- [ ] 1 tsp [espresso powder]{ ing="espresso-powder" }
- [ ] 1 tsp [salt]{ ing="salt" }
- [ ] 3 large [eggs]{ ing="egg" }
- [ ] 1 cup [all-purpose flour]{ ing="all-purpose-flour" }
- [ ] 2/3 cup [Dutch-process cocoa powder]{ ing="dutch-process-cocoa-powder" }
- [ ] 1/2 cup [semi-sweet chocolate chips]{ ing="semi-sweet-chocolate-chips" }
- [ ] [Nonstick cooking spray]{ ing="nonstick-cooking-spray" }

## Recipe

1. Preheat the oven to 350F
1. Add the [butter]{ ing="unsalted-butter" } and chopped [chocolate bar]{ ing="semi-sweet-chocolate-bar" } to a large microwave-safe bowl. Microwave in 15-second increments, stirring between each, until smooth. Let sit for 3 minutes to cool slightly
1. Add the granulated and [brown sugars]{ ing="brown-sugar" }, vanilla, [espresso powder]{ ing="espresso-powder" }, and [salt]{ ing="salt" }. Whisk to combine
1. Whisk in the [eggs]{ ing="egg" } one at a time until fully combined and glossy
1. Sift the [flour]{ ing="all-purpose-flour" } and [cocoa powder]{ ing="dutch-process-cocoa-powder" } into the bowl and fold in with a spatula until just combined. Fold in the [chocolate chips]{ ing="semi-sweet-chocolate-chips" }
1. Grease a 9-inch square baking pan. Spread the batter evenly in the pan
1. Bake for 35-40 minutes, until a toothpick inserted in the center comes out with a few moist crumbs attached
1. Let cool completely before cutting

## Notes

- For fudgier texture and shiny crust: heat butter and sugar together to 110-120F before mixing with eggs (technique from [King Arthur Baking](https://www.kingarthurbaking.com/recipes/fudge-brownies-recipe) ([wayback](http://web.archive.org/web/20260115000000*/https://www.kingarthurbaking.com/recipes/fudge-brownies-recipe)))
